Retain qualified allocation and masked-region layout policies.

The new adjacent AMDGPU EXEC-restore layout and edge-consumer-first allocation
policy interact to introduce loop copies and earlier waits in production
convolutions. Together they regress ArcFace by 32% and SCRFD by 11% on gfx1151.
Retain the preceding placement and linear-register preferences while preserving the new physical
register-view support, semantic live-segment alias checks and completion fixes.
Restoring only one policy leaves a reproducible regression.

Declared physical register views retain the newer consumer-first preference.
The assembly expectations below restore block placement and move one independent
scalar increment before its existing complete vector wait. No program,
reference result, tolerance, memory contract or alias-safety condition changes.
See docs/NATIVE-REFRESH.md and its raw paired qualification evidence.

